data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Refining Bias Mitigation**\n\nI'm now carefully examining the potential for selection bias in the experimental design. I've realized that using \"passing the gate\" as a criterion can skew the results, particularly when reporting findings. I'm focusing on ensuring external validity. Furthermore, my current focus is on a structured plan for evaluating the *portée* and generalizability of my claims.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 1714,"totalTokenCount": 11323,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 1714}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 9609,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-neon","responseId": "j-gCa97DNfejuMYP_OiYuAs"}

data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Refining Ensemble Bias Mitigation**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on mitigating potential bias within the experimental design, given question 1's impact. I've pinpointed that using the same validation set for both training and as a \"gate\" could lead to skewed results and over-fitting, undermining generalizability. My focus now is designing an external, separate validation set to evaluate the overall scope.\n\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 1714,"totalTokenCount": 11617,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 1714}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 9903,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-neon","responseId": "j-gCa97DNfejuMYP_OiYuAs"}

data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Refining Experimental Iterations**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the iterations of my experimental approach, particularly the use of *H* as a pass/fail criterion versus a disjoint validation set. I am now exploring the implications of statistical tests, specifically the difference-of-optimism test. I will ensure clarity in the response and also consider the certainty factor I'll use to communicate the confidence level.\n\nI'm also considering the use of *H*, to be consulted each cycle, by parts, once, or never, at the completion of the detection phase to ensure methodological correctness.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 1714,"totalTokenCount": 11907,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 1714}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 10193,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-neon","responseId": "j-gCa97DNfejuMYP_OiYuAs"}

