data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Refining Ensemble Audits**\n\nI'm now integrating an external cryptographic audit of $H$, performed with only a single decryption, to ensure its integrity after detector freezing. I'm focusing on simulating a Monte Carlo test, under the null hypothesis, to verify that a single consultation's false positive rate remains at or below α, to prevent repeated probing.\n\n\\n\\nI'm now refining the auditing strategy to ensure that the initial claim of low false positives holds after the experiment's completion. To avoid the bias from *peeking*, I've added a cryptographic audit of H, with a Monte Carlo simulation. My focus is on ensuring H is immutable to maintain the validity of the results.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 1714,"totalTokenCount": 12756,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 1714}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 11042,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-neon","responseId": "j-gCa97DNfejuMYP_OiYuAs"}

